{
  "section": "CRS-05",
  "name": "content-padding",
  "description": "Derived from the stated rules; not oracle evidence. Padding of a serialized content container before 1:1 or sender-key encryption: the content, then 0x80, then 0x00 bytes up to a total length of ceil((n+2)/80)*80 - 1, where n is the content length. Unpadding cases: the content is every byte before the final 0x80, which may be followed only by 0x00 bytes; other inputs are malformed (error).",
